02:20:44.310 --> 02:20:45.310
David Maisel: Mm-hmm.

02:20:45.310 --> 02:20:46.310
Tim Ferriss: That's wild.

02:20:46.310 --> 02:20:47.310
David Maisel: Yeah.

02:20:47.310 --> 02:20:49.720
And if there's no legacy, then it's just purely
new.

02:20:49.720 --> 02:20:52.890
You don't get into the geekiness like with
pipes.

02:20:52.890 --> 02:20:54.149
How was it done a hundred years ago?

02:20:54.149 --> 02:20:57.430
And look at this pipe, it's a collectible
or whatever, you know?

02:20:57.430 --> 02:20:58.680
You don't have all that.

02:20:58.680 --> 02:21:03.320
And if it's completely legacy, but it's so
big, then there's no thrill of discovery,

02:21:03.320 --> 02:21:04.320
right?

02:21:04.320 --> 02:21:05.320
Tim Ferriss: Yeah.

02:21:05.320 --> 02:21:07.050
David Maisel: So it's the balance on the scale
of those things.

02:21:07.050 --> 02:21:09.590
Tim Ferriss: You know who I think did a really
